    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 21—Miscellaneous",
    "Division 3—General",
    "21.24C  Period for doing certain acts—acts to which section 223A does not apply"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "21.24C",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r21.24C",
  "text": "For subsection 223A(7) of the Act, the following acts are prescribed: (a) an act done in opposition proceedings, other than the filing of a notice or request with the Trade Marks Office, under the following provisions: (i) Part 5, 9 or 21 of the Act; (ii) Part 5, 9, 17A or 21 of these Regulations; (b) an act done in relation to proceedings in a court or a tribunal; (c) the filing of a notice of opposition with a court under section 96 of the Act; (d) an act done under Part 13 or 16 of the Act; (e) an act done under Part 13, 16 or 20 of these Regulations.",
